# LTspice records absolute paths in every .log it writes. The ltspicelog clean
# filter reduces those paths to bare filenames as a log is staged, so a local
# username and folder layout never reach the repository. Rerunning a
# simulation restores the full paths in the working copy, but the staged and
# committed form stays clean, and the file no longer shows as modified.
#
# Enable it once per clone, from the repository root:
#   git config filter.ltspicelog.clean "sh tools/strip-ltspice-log-paths.sh"
#
# Git silently ignores the attribute when that config is absent, and logs would
# then be staged with full paths, so set it before committing a log.
*.log filter=ltspicelog

# Keep the shell scripts LF so Git for Windows can run them.
*.sh text eol=lf
